xecution evidence. Reject skeletal authoring plans: production@2.0, semantic fit decisions, visual grammar @1 with every scene, and character assembly @2 must be materially authored before write-phase02-authoring; no placeholder plan can pass the authoring writer. Depth-background composition is compatibility/explicit opt-in only, never the fresh default. If an approved legacy episode explicitly selects it, read references/depth-background-system.md and use phase02-execute-with-depth.mjs; otherwise preserve the primary scene-set and do not invent windows, perspective, shadows, gradients, or full-canvas room backgrounds. CONTEXT BUDGET: before each manifest step run orchestration/plan-step-context.mjs for the exact phase/step and active flags; load required references only for the current step, preserve mandatory receipts/validators and review gates. Do not load all Phase02 contracts or previous video packages upfront. Condense state handoff to source hashes, approval IDs and unresolved issues; re-read the primary file only when required. Context selection is advisory and cannot waive any required capability. CONTEXT RESUME: use read-only orchestration/context-capsule.mjs for short state handoffs. Conditional flags must be explicit; context plans cannot waive validators or approvals. SINGLE-SOURCE SCENE CONTEXT: use orchestration/derive-scene-context.mjs only for bounded scene references when working a scene; never copy full narration, design intents or whole plans into each handoff; read canonical source when modifying and do not skip any manifest gates. After Visual Compile, run orchestration/audit-creative-reuse.mjs for repetition review. Never force new SVG or silently block legitimate same-character/same-setting continuity. NARRATION RHYTHM: Fresh >=2.4.47 uses TONE_RHYTHM_DEFAULT and Narrative Plan 2.0; read references/narration-rhythm.md. Preserve narrator identity but choose delivery/energy/emotion/pace/emphasis by semantic beat, no fixed gắt baseline or required emotional sequence. Bind actual voice anchors after drafting and compile-narration-performance.mjs before resolved composition. Existing approved narration is immutable. Backend metadata is not proof of applied prosody; inspect runner voice-performance.json and listen to real takes. RELEASE 2.4.48: Zodiac remains Phase1 owner; Video Lab is conditional leaf guidance only. Verify actual live/source entry against loaded-entry-identity.json before fresh Evidence; stale cached instructions block. Compile bounded evidence and writer briefs, validate source lineage and plugin-use decisions, and commit Phase1 steps with expected state/source hashes and real receipts. Use draft/review context scopes, not imaginary independent agents. Fresh Story Object @2 must select a sign-specific metaphor, removal test, per-beat added meaning and relational payoff; object-only consequences are valid and conceptual instance lineage replaces same-ID assumptions. Phase3 has one production entrypoint with owned substages; preserve approved source/review lock context and return a ZIP-bound handoff receipt with actual runner/audio/temporal QA explicitly pending. No Video Lab default pipeline, advertising, word-count quotas or new assets-per-shot rule in production content. RELEASE 2.4.50: For new scoped episodes read references/episode-formats.md, set episode_selected before Evidence, carry research-scope and episode-scope, use Narrative 2.1 rather than a fake primary sign. Narrative 2.0 remains legacy-compatible and the same rhythm gates apply to 2.1. Support single_sign, exact element_group, editorial ranked_shortlist 2-5 and comparison 2-4; never default to all12. Bound source coverage, winner lenses, beat evidence ownership and actual narrated member review. Phase2 requires explicit episode-cast-plan and honest cover episode_id/label; Phase3 public --episode-scope uses the approved scope and stable episode job identity. Keep Job5 unchanged, no automatic editorial/user approval or media