+++ b/plugins/zodiac-video-pipeline/skills/zodiac-video-pipeline/references/asset-library-v4/selection-guide.md
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 # Visual Grammar v4 selection guide
 
-Per beat: choose one Frame Skeleton + one primary Mechanic, then bind existing entities. Scene Direction owns coordinates.
+Start with the approved **scene-set** (the stable wall/floor/frame stage). Per beat, choose one shot-layout (historically `Frame Skeleton`) + one primary Mechanic, then bind existing entities. Scene Direction owns coordinates. `frames/` remains the compatibility path for shot-layout metadata; it is not the scene-set library.
 
 For each ordinary character, choose identity once in `.authoring/character-assembly-plan.json`:
 `body_profile + hair_id + face_profile_id + outfit_id + accessory_id + stable variant_seed`.
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@ Each character state chooses only `pose_id + expression_id`. State-level identit
 Frame families: `single-character-focus`, `two-person-offset`, `prop-focus`, `reaction-closeup`, `caption-payoff`.
 Mechanics: `explain`, `react`, `show-object`, `offer-object`, `confront`, `reveal`, `payoff`.
 
-Choose structural cues only when the authored intent needs them. Archive-frame shots retain only the selected frame with wall/floor; room profiles do not instantiate extra cues. Structural cues stay separate from story props. Select a notebook, book, water bottle, backpack, pen, headset, tissue box or mirror only when narration calls for it.
+Choose structural cues only when the authored intent explicitly selects `selected_cues`. Fresh archive-frame/scene-set shots retain the selected outer frame with wall/floor and do not instantiate window/sofa/table/room cues. Optional `scene_accent` details stay inside the scene-set `wall_region`. Structural cues stay separate from story props. Select a notebook, book, water bottle, backpack, pen, headset, tissue box or mirror only when narration calls for it.
 
 Visual Grammar and Character Assembly plans are compile-time only and never cross the runtime boundary.
 
